네 컷 — an original exorcist short (1-bit Dither style, made with the Lemo-Opuscar style library)

Story and characters
- Original story, characters and dialogue. The mood of Korean urban-occult fiction is the inspiration; no characters, events or
  settings from any existing work are used. "사진관 24" is an invented shop; the 2003 missing-person poster is fiction.

Picture
- All imagery is generated by code in this folder (three.js scenes through a two-ink ordered-dither pipeline; the photo strips are
  rendered from the booth set and printed by error diffusion; the poster photo is a halftone screen). No photos, no image
  generation. The dither pipe and kit are adapted from the library's 1-bit Dither demo (pipe.js, kit.js), Lemo-Opuscar (MIT for code).
  three.js r170 (MIT).

Music and sound
- Original score composed and synthesized in music/score.py (numpy: bass clarinet, glockenspiel, Karplus–Strong pizzicato,
  bowed low strings, a detuned upright piano, brushes). No samples, no recordings.
- Sound effects and room tone synthesized in mix.py with the library's core/audio/sfx.py and numpy. No recordings.

Voices
- Google Cloud Text-to-Speech, Chirp 3: HD — ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Kore (서하), ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Aoede (지은),
  ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Leda (the booth's voice), ko-KR-Chirp3-HD-Despina (the girl in the photographs), under the user's Google Cloud
  account and its terms.
- Fish Audio community voice model "70대 노스님" (a36c3dd96a79431f87072de815559e97, free model s2.1-pro-free) for 무진, under the
  user's Fish Audio account and its terms.
- Speech check: faster-whisper small (MIT) via the library's core/tts/asr_check.py.

